  "review_notes": [
    "All four required Stata stages succeeded with process returncode 0, native completion code 0, no detected Stata r() errors, and fresh declared outputs. The controlled receipt records unchanged original input hashes, plan hash and runtime policy hash.",
    "The source captures contain 59 author-native estimation fits total: 22 for Tables 3-8, 21 for Tables 9B-9D, 10 for F-statistics, and 6 for Figures 2-4; the F-statistics stage also ran 10 native test commands. The figure stage ran six coefplots and exported six PDFs.",
    "Thirty-eight fits reported “Warning: VCV matrix was non-positive semi-definite; adjustment from Cameron, Gelbach & Miller applied”: 22 in Tables 3-8, 10 in F-statistics, and 6 in Figures 2-4. The author specifications and Stata’s automatic adjustment were retained; no covariance, estimator, standard-error or inference repair was made. Table 9B-9D showed no such warning.",
    "The six generated PDFs are each one page at 540 x 324 pt in landscape orientation. Rendered views show the source axis labels, ticks, confidence intervals and lines clearly, with no clipping or text overlap. The source does not identify panel letters; the output names use figure topic and estimator.",
    "This is only the supplied final-data Stata branch, lines 37-428 with source blank terminator line 429 retained. Table 2B remains a gap because corrtbl is unresolved. Appendix III prediction, raw-data preparation, SAS descriptive/Appendix III code, Table 1, Table 9A and outputs absent from this branch are outside scope; this is not a full-paper reproduction claim.",
    "The frozen one-row input metadata probes support selected-field presence and readability only; they do not establish full population/year coverage. The exact four packaged author-prepared DTA inputs were used without modifying their bytes.",
    "The stage capture logs and per-stage summaries are retained under runtime/stages; runtime/run.json is the shared receipt referenced by each stage result. The exact table and PDF output hashes are recorded in artifacts."
  ],
